## 0. Mathematical Foundations — Statistics and Analysis

The polynomial encoding module operates over `GF(2¹⁶)` using the `GF16`
type from `encoding/gf.rs`. All polynomial arithmetic (addition,
multiplication, subtraction, division of coefficients and evaluation
points) reduces to GF(2¹⁶) operations, whose foundations are in
[`Spqr/Math/Gf16/`](../../Spqr/Math/Gf16/) (see [`Plan_gf`](Plan_gf)).

On top of the GF(2¹⁶) layer, the polynomial verification needs
algebraic facts about polynomials over GF(2¹⁶): Horner evaluation,
products of linear factors, Lagrange basis polynomials, and
characteristic-2 identities. These are organised across the modular
file tree at [`Spqr/Math/Poly/`](../../Spqr/Math/Poly/) with helper
list lemmas in [`Spqr/Math/List.lean`](../../Spqr/Math/List.lean).

