## 3. Function Descriptions

### Constants

- **`MAX_STORED_POLYNOMIAL_DEGREE_V1` (35)** [C1] — Maximum degree of a
  polynomial that will be stored/serialized for Protocol V1. A degree-35
  polynomial has 36 coefficients.
- **`MAX_INTERMEDIATE_POLYNOMIAL_DEGREE_V1` (36)** [C2] — Maximum degree
  during intermediate Lagrange interpolation; one higher than the stored
  maximum.
- **`COMPLETE_POINTS_POLYS_{1,3,5,30,34,36}`** [C3–C8] — Precomputed
  arrays of Lagrange basis polynomials for the listed numbers of
  complete points.
- **`CHUNK_SIZE` (32)** [C9] — Size of an encoding chunk in bytes.
- **`NUM_POLYS` (16)** [C10] — `CHUNK_SIZE / 2` — number of polynomials
  tracked per chunk (each `GF16` element is 2 bytes).
- **`PolyConst::ZEROS`** [C11] — `PolyConst<N>` with all coefficients
  `GF16::ZERO`; used as the initial value of `PolyConst` arrays.

### Pt (Cartesian Point)

- **`Pt::serialize`** [F1] — Serializes a `Pt { x, y }` into four
  big-endian bytes `[x_hi, x_lo, y_hi, y_lo]`.
- **`Pt::deserialize`** [F2] — Inverse of F1: reads two `u16` big-endian
  values into a `Pt`.
- **`{impl Ord}::cmp`** [F3] — Delegates to `partial_cmp` + `unwrap`.
- **`{impl PartialOrd}::partial_cmp`** [F4] — `u16` comparison on
  `self.x.value`.
- **`{impl PartialEq}::eq`** [F5] — `u16` equality on `self.x.value`
  (y-coordinate ignored).

### Poly (Dynamic Polynomial)

- **`Poly::zero(capacity)`** [F6] — Empty polynomial with given `Vec`
  capacity.
- **`Poly::lagrange_interpolate(pts)`** [F7] — Returns `p` with
  `p(ptsᵢ.x) = ptsᵢ.y`; uses prepare/complete strategy in O(N²) work.
- **`Poly::lagrange_interpolate_prepare(pts)`** [F8] — Builds
  `∏ᵢ (x − ptsᵢ.x)` from largest coefficient down; template for F10.
- **`Poly::mult_xdiff_assign_trailing(start, d)`** [F9] — Multiplies
  `self[start..]` by `(x − d)` in place; propagates carry into
  `self[start-1]`.
- **`Poly::lagrange_interpolate_complete(pts, i)`** [F10] — Divides
  the product polynomial by `(x − ptsᵢ.x)` and rescales so that
  `f(ptsᵢ.x) = ptsᵢ.y`.
- **`Poly::lagrange_interpolate_pt(pts, i)`** [F11] —
  prepare + complete + remove leading zero; used as a fallback for
  encoding.
- **`Poly::add_assign(other)`** [F12] — Coefficient-wise addition,
  extending `self` if `other` is longer.
- **`Poly::mult_assign(m)`** [F13] — Scales every coefficient by `m`
  via `gf::parallel_mult`.
- **`Poly::compute_at(x)`** [F14] — Evaluates the polynomial at `x` by
  building powers of `x` and summing `aᵢ·xⁱ`. Marked
  `#[hax_lib::opaque]` due to `zip`.
- **`Poly::lagrange_sum(pts, polys)`** [F15] —
  `Σᵢ polysᵢ · ptsᵢ.y` to combine Lagrange basis polynomials.
- **`Poly::from_complete_points(pts)`** [F16] — Uses precomputed
  `COMPLETE_POINTS_POLYS_*` for sizes 1, 3, 5, 30, 34, 36, falling back
  to F11 otherwise.
- **`Poly::serialize`** [F17] — Big-endian `u16` byte stream of each
  coefficient.
- **`Poly::deserialize(buf)`** [F18] — Inverse of F17; errors on empty
  or odd-length input.

### PolyConst (Fixed-Size Const Polynomial)

- **`PolyConst::lagrange_interpolate_pt(pts, i)`** [F19] —
  Const-evaluable Lagrange interpolation for a single point using
  `const_sub`, `const_mul`, `const_div`.
- **`PolyConst::mult(m)`** [F20] — Const scalar multiplication.
- **`PolyConst::mult_xdiff(d)`** [F21] — Const multiplication by
  `(x − d)`, distributed as `x·poly − d·poly`.
- **`PolyConst::to_poly`** [F22] — Lifts a `PolyConst<N>` to a dynamic
  `Poly` via `to_vec`.

### Free Functions

- **`const_polys_to_polys(cps)`** [F23] — Maps `to_poly` over an array
  of `PolyConst<N>` to produce a `Vec<Poly>`.
- **`lagrange_polys_for_complete_points<N>()`** [F24] — Precomputes
  the `N` Lagrange basis polynomials for `{(0,1), (1,1), …, (N−1,1)}`;
  initializes the `COMPLETE_POINTS_POLYS_*` constants.

### PolyEncoder

- **`PolyEncoder::get_encoder_state`** [F25] — Returns a reference to
  the internal `EncoderState` (`Points` or `Polys`).
- **`PolyEncoder::into_pb`** [F26] — Serializes encoder state into
  `proto::PolynomialEncoder`.
- **`PolyEncoder::from_pb`** [F27] — Validates and reconstructs an
  encoder from protobuf.
- **`PolyEncoder::point_at(poly, idx)`** [F28] — Returns the `GF16`
  value at `(poly, idx)`; converts `Points → Polys` if needed.
- **`PolyEncoder::encode_bytes_base(msg)`** [F29] — Splits a message
  into 2-byte `GF16` elements distributed round-robin across 16
  polynomial point arrays.
- **`PolyEncoder::chunk_at(idx)`** [F30] — Generates the chunk at the
  given index by evaluating each of the 16 polynomials.
- **`PolyEncoder::{into_pb_test,from_pb_test}`** [F31–F32] —
  Test-utility wrappers.
- **`{impl Encoder}::encode_bytes(msg)`** [F33] — Delegates to F29.
- **`{impl Encoder}::next_chunk`** [F34] — Calls F30 and increments
  the index.

### PolyDecoder

- **`PolyDecoder::get_pts_needed`** [F35] — Returns `self.pts_needed`.
- **`PolyDecoder::necessary_points(poly)`** [F36] —
  `pts_needed / 16 + (1 if poly < pts_needed % 16 else 0)`.
- **`PolyDecoder::new_with_poly_count(len_bytes, _polys)`** [F37] —
  `pts_needed = len_bytes / 2`, empty `SortedSet<Pt>` arrays.
- **`PolyDecoder::into_pb` / `from_pb`** [F38–F39] — Protobuf
  serialization round-trip.
- **`PolyDecoder::{into_pb_test,from_pb_test}`** [F40–F41] —
  Test-utility wrappers.
- **`{impl Decoder}::new(len_bytes)`** [F42] — Delegates to F37.
- **`{impl Decoder}::add_chunk(chunk)`** [F43] — Adds the 16 `GF16`
  values to the per-polynomial `SortedSet<Pt>` arrays.
- **`{impl Decoder}::decoded_message`** [F44] — Reconstructs the
  message via direct lookup + Lagrange interpolation. **Opaque axiom.**

### Test Functions (not extracted)

- **F45–F50** — Unit tests for round-tripping, interpolation, and
  protobuf serialization. Not extracted by Aeneas.

